{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2evpa75pvuail5rlpgg27vwpoolexbmvlzekwowuaazb3ldfiz5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Clean build with no warnings, and the completion gate is met.\n\n## What the C library is\n`c_src/` is a single translation unit (`src/lib.c`, globbed by CMake) — a trimmed-down *tinyc2*-style 2D collision library. `include/lib.h` declares only `circle_collide`, but the `.so` exports 12 symbols because none of the helpers are `static`. No namespace-renaming macros are present, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Symbol parity (the definition of done)\n`nm -D` on the C `.so` vs. my Rust `.so` — **diff is empty in both directions**, all 12 exports present with identical names:\n\n`c2V`, `c2Mulvs`, `c2Maxv`, `c2Minv`, `c2Clampv`, `c2Sub`, `c2Dot`, `c2CircletoCircle`, `c2CircletoAABB`, `c2CircletoCapsule`, `c2Collided`, `circle_collide`\n\n## Files written (outside `c_src/`, which is byte-for-byte untouched)\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `src/lib.rs` — all 12 functions with `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`, `#[repr(C)]` structs (`c2v`, `c2Circle`, `c2AABB`, `c2Capsule`), and `c_int`/`*const c_void` FFI types.\n\n## Behavior fidelity\nI built a `dlopen`-based differential harness loading both `.so`s side by side and comparing **raw bit patterns** (not `==`, so signed zeros and NaN payloads count) over: exhaustive pairs of 33 interesting floats (incl. ±0, ±∞, NaN, subnormals, values straddling every fixed shape boundary), a dense 3-D sweep of `circle_collide` across the region containing all three fixed shapes, invalid `c2Collided` type tags (−3..7), and 400 k random runs using raw random bit patterns.\n\n**Result: 2,534,633 checks, 0 mismatches.**\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. **A real bug found by the fuzzer, then fixed to match C.** With signaling-NaN inputs, `c2Dot` differed in NaN *payload*: GCC's `addss` keeps the second product's payload, LLVM's kept the first. I verified the ground truth against the compiled C library and made the propagation explicit (`nan_ordered`) rather than relying on codegen luck — ordinary values take the plain arithmetic path, so this is a no-op for non-NaN inputs.\n2. **C quirks preserved, not fixed.** `c2Collided` unconditionally reinterprets `A` as a `c2Circle` regardless of any type tag (only `B` is dispatched) — reproduced as-is. `c2Maxv`/`c2Minv` use literal `?:` selection rather than `f32::max`/`min`, since those differ on NaN."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":198,"cache_read_input_tokens":39318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":198,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d954a7d-bb70-49d9-8d8d-d2ced2e7fb21","uuid":"bd5250a1-2e05-426d-b263-39dc85597eb6","timestamp":"2026-08-20T02:49:09.835Z"}
